---
/**
 * ============================================================================
 * PROJECTS SECTION (Projects.astro)
 * ============================================================================
 * What this component does:
 * - Highlights your key software projects in a clean two-column responsive grid.
 *
 * HOW TO MAINTAIN:
 * - To edit an existing project: update the name, link, image, or bullet points
 *   inside any <article class="project-card">.
 * - To add a new project: copy an entire <article class="project-card"> block
 *   and paste it inside <div class="projects-grid">.
 * - Images can be placed in `public/` and linked via `<img src="/your-image.png" />`.
 * ============================================================================
 */
---

<section id="resume-projects" class="story-section container">
  <h2>Projects</h2>
  <p>
    This section highlights projects that reflect how I think, build, and
    deliver practical solutions.
  </p>
  <div class="projects-grid">
    <!-- PROJECT CARD 1 -->
    <article class="project-card">
      <div class="project-media" role="img" aria-label="TaskLocal Trust and Safety">
        <p class="project-media-label">
          <span>TaskLocal</span>
          <span>Trust &amp; Safety</span>
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="project-content">
        <h3>TaskLocal Trust &amp; Safety</h3>
        <p class="project-links">
          <a
            href="https://github.com/justin-day-pursuit/TaskLocal-TrustAndSafety"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >View on GitHub</a
          >
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            A marketplace reviewer clears reported reviews from one dashboard
            and reads a morning briefing of what changed.
          </li>
          <li>
            Emails, phone numbers, and other identifiers are stripped before
            Gemini sees the text, and chart numbers stay computed in the app.
            Built with Next.js, TypeScript, Supabase, and Gemini.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </article>

    <!-- PROJECT CARD 2 -->
    <article class="project-card">
      <div class="project-media">
        <img
          src="/professor-fritts.png"
          alt="Professor Fritts poster: a stylized portrait beside a glass building, with the words Renewable Energy Planning"
        />
      </div>
      <div class="project-content">
        <h3>Professor Fritts</h3>
        <p class="project-links">
          <a
            href="https://professor-fritts-clean-energy.vercel.app"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >Live demo</a
          >
          <a
            href="https://github.com/justin-day-pursuit/professor-fritts-clean-energy"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >GitHub</a
          >
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            A planner for NYC building managers facing Local Law 97. A building
            and a budget become three clean-energy scenarios.
          </li>
          <li>
            Every figure is labeled fact, estimate, assumption, or
            recommendation. Built with Next.js, FastAPI, Django, and Claude.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
